# Implement Magic Dictionary

**LeetCode Problem:** [Implement Magic Dictionary](https://leetcode.com/problems/implement-magic-dictionary/)

## Approach: Trie + Character Replacement

1. Implement a Trie data structure where each node contains an array of 26 child pointers and a boolean `isEndOfWord` to mark the end of a word.
2. In `buildDict()`, insert all dictionary words into the Trie.
3. In `search()`, iterate through each character of the given word.
4. Replace the current character with every other lowercase English letter except the original character.
5. For each modified word, use `solve()` to check whether it exists in the Trie.
6. If any modified word exists in the dictionary, return `true`; otherwise, return `false`.

## Complexity Analysis

Let:
- \(N\) = Number of words in the dictionary.
- \(L\) = Maximum length of a dictionary word.
- \(M\) = Length of the search word.

- **Time Complexity:**
  - `buildDict()`: \(O(N \times L)\)
  - `search()`: \(O(26 \times M^2)\), since each character replacement creates a modified string and checks it in the Trie.

- **Space Complexity:** \(O(N \times L)\) for storing the Trie.

## Code

```cpp
class MagicDictionary {
public:
    struct trieNode {
        bool isEndOfWord;
        trieNode* children[26];
    };

    trieNode* getNode() {
        trieNode* newNode = new trieNode();
        newNode->isEndOfWord = false;
        for(int i = 0; i < 26; i++)
            newNode->children[i] = NULL;
        return newNode;
    }

    trieNode* root;

    bool solve(string& searchWord) {
        trieNode* node = root;

        for(const char& ch : searchWord) {
            int idx = ch - 'a';
            if(node->children[idx] == NULL)
                return false;
            node = node->children[idx];
        }

        return node->isEndOfWord == true;
    }

    MagicDictionary() {
        root = getNode();
    }

    void buildDict(vector<string> dictionary) {
        for(const string& s : dictionary) {
            trieNode* node = root;

            for(const char& ch : s) {
                int idx = ch - 'a';
                if(node->children[idx] == NULL)
                    node->children[idx] = getNode();
                node = node->children[idx];
            }

            node->isEndOfWord = true;
        }
    }

    bool search(string searchWord) {
        for(int i = 0; i < searchWord.length(); i++) {
            char pivot = searchWord[i];

            for(char ch = 'a'; ch <= 'z'; ch++) {
                if(pivot == ch) continue;

                string temp = searchWord;
                temp[i] = ch;

                if(solve(temp)) return true;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }
};
```

## Key Concept

The Trie efficiently stores dictionary words and allows checking whether a word exists after modifying exactly one character. The search considers all possible single-character replacements.
